# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Both are read by Expo CLI and by
# `expo run:android`; `.env.local` wins, and it is gitignored so it is the safe place for keys.
#
# Leave EVERY line here commented. `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the bundle at BUILD time, so
# an uncommented value is baked into whatever is built next — including a release APK. A stale
# LAN IP sat in this file for exactly that reason and produced release builds that only worked
# on one person's desk. With nothing set, `src/config.ts` falls back to the deployed API, which
# is what a release build should always talk to.

# Your own Mac's LAN IP, for a physical device pointed at a local backend. Never localhost:
# the phone resolves that to itself. Find yours with `ipconfig getifaddr en0`.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://YOUR.LAN.IP.HERE:8000

# Lets the debug build talk to that backend over plain HTTP. Local development only.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_CLEARTEXT=true
